{"id": "lem-counting-measure-on-a-discrete-group", "batch": "10", "verdict": "accepted-current", "mathematical_evidence": "Every subset is Borel in the discrete topology; compact sets are finite and finite sets compact. Inner regularity forces any Haar measure to have mass c on each point and c·counting on all sets. Positivity and finiteness of c follow from nonzeroness, regularity and compact-singleton finiteness. Nonnegative integrals equal the supremum of finite sums; absolute integrability gives complex summability. No arbitrary-index choice is used.", "current_item_raw_sha256": "a79ea22c5393aba731bc016a5081b386ec5b4937742d023d3b0d88b5700ce10f", "current_item_guard_sha256": "a0c4c0176596c841416df14f6a995bfe92055fe0fbc43397b26bf926d9f253bd", "current_item_surface_sha256": "cf9207921407e614488233838717ad2c0dcd632c58be6395584682f01423e0ae", "current_claim_section_sha256": "63182425d4f3fe7a8c6283bacdab280ef508ffa2e772a024253a2a9e8b802620", "current_proof_section_sha256": "5dacabd470a42673a5f6472c91e4f17d227c71c7d602f4d987fd39d58ca6ccce", "load_bearing_suppliers": [{"id": "def-left-haar-integral-and-left-haar-measure", "raw_sha256": "981def24417b83bc3a6592a0ffc979a15fae43f17c1f8a121d30a3aabe6c3b51"}, {"id": "prop-counting-measure-is-a-measure", "raw_sha256": "412626a04ed96bfa64bc16230745f0c4aac0b3949b01fc39f441acbb491549bc"}, {"id": "def-square-summable-family-on-an-arbitrary-index-set", "raw_sha256": "b5a0df845af9f1a9eba72910affece51da2100c1a9762366e0211aaaaa4053bc"}, {"id": "def-nonnegative-lebesgue-integral", "raw_sha256": "989fec7df5d1b99753334fc74e76a2a0bc44c515ff4a10bb7dce3efa69293972"}], "prior_auditor_author": "step3b-pair-the-modular-function-and-l1-group-algebras-375300b9cb01adc2", "prior_auditor_input_sha256": "2f4553dfadf0fd19ffcfd78f4f16c4f0dbcceff5acbe263d8742e623b2534b07", "prior_owner_decision": null, "direct_consumer_disposition": null, "checks": "focused precheck (proof items), rendercheck, depcheck, fwdcheck, validate-plan; strict contracts for sco