{"id": "lem-the-closed-disk-is-a-manifold-with-boundary", "batch": "16", "verdict": "repaired-current", "mathematical_evidence": "The Möbius boundary chart is a homeomorphism from the punctured disk to the closed upper half-plane; its imaginary part is (1−|w|²)/|q+w|² and the inverse is q(i−u)/(i+u). Corrected a domain assertion that had included u=−i, where the inverse is undefined, and removed a false nonzero assertion at w=0. Interior charts, Hausdorffness, second countability and connectedness remain sound.", "current_item_raw_sha256": "6f5517d2c6427ee19910a7b9932d422677da76d295bad540f7c142602c9c28b0", "current_item_guard_sha256": "d94a1dfe6465bd3f244d7cf5ba4e706b52025ccbb88d3556a73867dcbada52cf", "current_item_surface_sha256": "36538226b6ec3dae2a57c9b5e596994bbf4e7e8f153ee39fdab0e304e846b1d4", "current_claim_section_sha256": "96dfde38a50431b8c5bc49964f966da55f4522d4a507255dfc293ec41cd4be85", "current_proof_section_sha256": "76af62fbcc3a15735763cf388acc96cf61736e9def3465c5485859673491edf2", "load_bearing_suppliers": [{"id": "def-topological-manifold-with-boundary", "raw_sha256": "6b4aa3c9892d149a8f1cfd4d749a04e8c6cbc12ec4fb96e366f18562172a75a2"}, {"id": "def-euclidean-upper-half-space-and-its-boundary", "raw_sha256": "493fd762e1c372bd32bfab5daff78d735117e3acdc9f38223fd8d03971b5766c"}, {"id": "lem-complex-conjugation-and-modulus-laws", "raw_sha256": "1c39322a5f76e70d991e68270bd84935cb132cc04452a48af1e4f56e21221d39"}], "prior_auditor_author": "step3b-pair-ordered-and-unordered-configuration-spaces-b46560cd56c26c99", "prior_auditor_input_sha256": "66fce876d5ba37ba06b28bf327296e37078edc250b7af6f1bc72b01ad7171197", "prior_owner_decision": null, "direct_consumer_disposition": null, "checks": "focused precheck (proof items), rendercheck, depcheck, fwdcheck, validate-plan; strict contracts for scoped items in batches 3/6/10/16"}
{"id": "lem-ag-base-change-of-standard-smooth-presentations", "batch": "3", "verdict": "repaired-current", "mathematical_evidence": "Polynomial quotient and localization universal properties give inverse R′-algebra maps; coefficient change carries the Jacobian minor to a unit and preserves the derivative matrix. Corrected proof step 3.1: S→S′ is an R-algebra map, not an R′-algebra map, before applying the R-algebra tensor coproduct.", "current_item_raw_sha256": "3f93a126e60c13d905cdc29d49890ac2fe916e9629097b360da7f1ec3154178c", "current_item_guard_sha256": "f566b4891283af454cfee48894744f36a37741ebb83f67aa6b78bad5eb874b42", "current_item_surface_sha256": "05b22e93bf94a98822cafc83c94bfef16cbd40edb04c95d65d1f4b89d7b91909", "current_claim_section_sha256": "43fe4d3cb6a942f3e4f3465b42412ecab2a4213b0cb23c8c1ddfa2adae8a74a9", "current_proof_section_sha256": "fc9dddb5670959ac09a7e1cb491639fe731a8d844113c588dcc566e1aa3489ce", "load_bearing_suppliers": [{"id": "def-ag-standard-smooth-algebra", "raw_sha256": "913d7b4acf419dbf29e0709a7177c925d8301231b978c3c484c7f1559d7384f9"}, {"id": "lem-ag-polynomial-quotient-differentials", "raw_sha256": "9d8eff40bce344cd86541baddc85d97854cae61e1a14c11bf229434d1c049af9"}, {"id": "thm-coproduct-property-of-tensor-products-of-commutative-algebras", "raw_sha256": "44ca3206c02a82771e997b89dfbbb91da299abee24491cd19203043be3ef90b3"}], "prior_auditor_author": "step3b-pair-algebraic-differentials-separability-and-smooth-local-presentations-980fc793d0c33b58", "prior_auditor_input_sha256": "7401f0fdddf99a5b0b2c26a882128cd67c02e88f03ee9cc6b02a2cb6ec6e1a97", "prior_owner_decision": null, "direct_consumer_disposition": null, "checks": "focused precheck (proof items), rendercheck, depcheck, fwdcheck, validate-plan; strict contracts for scoped items in batches 3/6/10/16"}
{"id": "lem-ag-standard-smooth-fibre-regular-parameters", "batch": "3", "verdict": "accepted-current", "mathematical_evidence": "The derivative map on m/m² is well defined by Leibniz; invertibility of the Jacobian minor makes the f_j classes independent. Under explicit AC, the regular polynomial localization and basis-extension suppliers give a regular parameter system beginning with f_j; its initial segment is regular and leaves a regular quotient of dimension dim A−c.", "current_item_raw_sha256": "8e850a39e8aecd1191a308c8dbdddf96a006a08b8ff7e400c5cc54c6df95e04e", "current_item_guard_sha256": "65385c0cecdbb28c6ed2d0d19803103bae66d5078026b8d10db31484936b5185", "current_item_surface_sha256": "792a9ffa8d8b33acaff3422f4c604dac5d8b76f6601723f083ebdb79d73a27dc", "current_claim_section_sha256": "908673ff5b80ad78cf11191f15c8f37b6db993bfedbb1e911b9a4692cf1eae7a", "current_proof_section_sha256": "c0af846cbe04a1826965c97d63a3e10693a4d23ea06a6078daf62741e5032315", "load_bearing_suppliers": [{"id": "thm-localisation-and-polynomial-extension-of-regular-rings", "raw_sha256": "a8aa0ba77f8657b7356f9225a84c5f94f722e1f921d873d0033d579742c11e6a"}, {"id": "lem-regular-system-of-parameters-equivalent-basis", "raw_sha256": "61e533b7f763dabe523558ad8761fc6446bbfd2deb7a87e01c9db0c4f0ede534"}, {"id": "thm-regular-local-rings-are-domains-and-cohen-macaulay", "raw_sha256": "703bd11c57ac123049d6293e4da5b49242fb27e7a6ceadc0e24841729a7ec5a1"}, {"id": "def-axiom-of-choice", "raw_sha256": "9c045248c142fcf687fdc3c5d25d8b3890ac08d1eca8b4e6d71bb00a4eb6ff58"}], "prior_auditor_author": "step3b-pair-algebraic-differentials-separability-and-smooth-local-presentations-980fc793d0c33b58", "prior_auditor_input_sha256": "0ca676293a59f3f1bc3369c9c7ac2ba4baf713a3b8b57bb1dea754964290c5f2", "prior_owner_decision": null, "direct_consumer_disposition": null, "checks": "focused precheck (proof items), rendercheck, depcheck, fwdcheck, validate-plan; strict contracts for scoped items in batches 3/6/10/16"}
